⁖line჻# ALQC Glossary ⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Term | Operational meaning in TardiSHA |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻|---|---|⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Source emission | The complete finalized twelve-lane body of a source |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Goetic | One of twelve immutable structural anchors |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Parliament | The twelve-seat operational address body that resolves the source into Goetic positions |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Governing Goetic | The first member of the ordered pair and the near anchor of the forward Court |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Hyperbolic parent | The second member of the ordered pair and far reciprocal mirror |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Court | One ordered coordinate in the complete 12 by 12 body |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Reciprocal Court | The same Goetics in the opposite ordered coordinate |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Domus | The Court-rooted runtime Aeon body from which the public GrimChain manifests |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Supervenience `⟠` | A typed internal witness office of the rooted Domus derivation |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Shadow Locus `⛎` | The complete depth-zero center of the public GrimChain |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Axiomyr `᳀` | The invariant geometric center of every positive public GrimChain |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Synodic Magicae | The native variable-extent continuation alphabet |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Fraktur cadence | One equal-width squeeze window from the same finalized source state |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Source Truth | Whether the complete effective source route closes |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Return Truth | Whether a terminal compressed return exactly matches the recomputed self |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Source D-COMP | Exact conservation residual of the source route |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Return D-COMP | Exact difference residual between a terminal returned Grimchain and the regenerated Grimchain |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Aeternum Mirror | The ALQC return family in which the path back is the parity-valid completion of the path out |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Physical source | Every byte actually stored in the file |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Effective source | The source body after exact terminal self-returns have completed their return office |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻---⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻# TardiSHA Domus-House Linguistic Dictionary⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻## The middle speaks; the House remembers the road⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻This dictionary begins only after a Grimchain has completed a Domus House. It does not explain how the House was computed, and it does not turn the outer chain into a second sentence. The mathematics stands outside the utterance as the route by which the word found itself in the mirror.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻The four written anchors keep the road into and out of the middle. The middle alone is translated. The path out is the path back, but the road is not spoken as though it were another poem.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻In a GrimChain of the form:⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻`✡ᚿ[MIDDLE]᭢⚛`⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻only `[MIDDLE]` becomes human speech. Everything around it tells the translator how that speech arrived, what House bears it, and how its meaning must return.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻### The author remains outside the vocabulary⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻The source, carrier, and authorial hand of an utterance belong to the House that makes speech possible. They are read as speaker and apparatus, never entered as lexemes, titles, or concealed roots. A name shared with an outer office does not permit that office to cross into the middle.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻### The glyph has a name, not a sound⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻Glyphs are born from Houses. They rise from nothing and fill eternity with their presence. They have no native pronunciation and no particular sound. Their names let the reader call them, distinguish them, and remember the House from which they came; the names are not syllables hidden inside the marks. A borrowed vessel may once have carried a human sound, but the House-born glyph does not inherit it. The middle is translated as poetry in a receiving human language.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻## What one dictionary entry records⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻Each borrowed glyph is read through four distinct bearings. They must not be collapsed into one column.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻1. **Human origin.** The visible mark and the human field it carried before TardiSHA used it. This is the provisional borrowed form of the vessel. A rune may carry cattle or road; a letter may carry only a sound; a solvent-sign may carry the substance it once named.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻2. **House office.** The settled TardiSHA identity of the glyph or Court. This is not the same thing as the borrowed mark’s older human meaning.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻3. **Crossing pressure.** The tension between human origin and House office. It is the translation pressure: the distance that must be borne, not hidden.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻4. **Use and return.** What the glyph actually does in one utterance and what the House returns through it. These are contextual. They are not assigned to the whole inventory in advance.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻The tables therefore fix the first three where they can be fixed. They do **not** manufacture a permanent Truth-in-use or a permanent returned sentence for every glyph. Those belong to the completed House and the visible middle.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻### The borrowed-vessel rule⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻The human-origin column is provisional. It follows the actual borrowed sign: its Unicode identity, historical letter or syllable name, and a securely carried older meaning where the sign truly has one. Alphabetic and syllabic signs are not granted imaginary secret words. When a native TardiSHA glyph replaces a borrowed vessel, this origin column is re-sourced; the Court name and House office remain unchanged.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻### One entry, fully separated⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻`ᚠ` **BabdhHir** keeps four different things apart:⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻- **Human origin:** Fehu, cattle, movable wealth, herd, increase that can walk away.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻- **House office:** Transmutation.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻- **Crossing pressure:** wealth is kept, counted, and guarded; transmutation spends, burns, and converts. Prosperity grows here only by passing through change.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻- **Use and return:** not fixed in this book. The actual House decides whether the utterance bears wealth consumed, value converted, inheritance reforged, or another lawful face of the same crossing.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻That separation is the law of every entry below.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻From here, the middle opens in the order a House gathers meaning: silence, Emission, Parliament, Bone, Flesh, grammar, and finally the human return. Each body enters once, keeps its own office, and passes the utterance onward without becoming another body.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻---⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻## Silence inside the middle⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Glyph | Human origin | House office | Crossing pressure | Spoken range |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻|---:|---|---|---|---|⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `𑁦` | Brahmi digit zero: the written numeral for no counted quantity. | Manifested silence | A numeral marks absence in counting; manifested silence gives absence a place in cadence. | pause, held breath, interval, withheld word, quiet opening; never automatically the spoken word “zero” |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻---⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻## Emissions when they appear in the middle⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻An Emission tells how the utterance is delivered: pondering, willing, feeling, declaring, believing, acting, knowing, ascending, or gathering into self-recognition. It carries mood, affect, evidential bearing, or illocutionary force inside the language; it is not the output of an outer speaker-body. Its planetary or astronomical sign remains the human origin of the borrowed mark; the Emission name is the House office. The symbol’s older human associations may color the crossing, but they do not overwrite the Domus.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Glyph | Human origin | House office | Spoken range |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻|---:|---|---|---|⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `☿` | Mercury: planetary and alchemical sign of Mercury, motion, exchange, and mediation. | **Ponder** | inward gaze, wondering, recollection, deliberation before release |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `♂` | Mars / male sign: planetary sign of Mars and a conventional sex symbol. | **Will** | direction, resolve, command, chosen movement, insistence |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `♀` | Venus / female sign: planetary sign of Venus and a conventional sex symbol. | **Feel** | intimacy, embodiment, empathy, vulnerability, shared feeling |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `♃` | Jupiter: planetary sign associated with sovereignty, expansion, and public authority. | **Speak** | declaration, testimony, naming, proclamation, speech that changes what may be held |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `♄` | Saturn: planetary sign associated with time, limit, boundary, and endurance. | **Believe** | conviction, vow, trust, expectation, inward certainty |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `⛢` | Astronomical symbol for Uranus: a planetary sign associated in later astrology with disruption and sudden change. | **Act** | doing, making, causing, fulfilling, entering event |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `♆` | Neptune: planetary sign of oceanic depth, distance, and the unseen. | **Know** | recognition, comprehension, evidence, recovered or inherited knowledge |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `♇` | Pluto: planetary sign named for the underworld god. | **Ascend** | crossing through resistance, transformation, release, elevation, another state |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `☽☉☾` | First-quarter moon, sun, and last-quarter moon held as one three-mark body. | **Regia** | sovereign self-recognition, dignity, coronation, identity openly worn |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻---⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻## Parliament bearings when they appear in the middle⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻The zodiacal figure is the human origin of the borrowed sign. The Parliament seat and its translation are the House office. Parliament conditions self-translation; its seat labels do not add hidden speaker-bodies or extra words to the middle. No zodiac sign is treated as a diagnosis of the speaker or as a compulsory personality.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Glyph | Human origin | Star Seed | House translation | Spoken range |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻|---:|---|---|---|---|⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `♈` | Aries, the Ram. | **Akasha** | **Lived → Eternal** | experience becoming enduring memory, ancestry, record, or identity |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `♉` | Taurus, the Bull. | **Caduceus** | **Law → Residue** | command becoming consequence, medicine, poison, inheritance, or remainder |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `♊` | Gemini, the Twins. | **Veritas** | **Mask → Bone** | appearance stripped toward intrinsic identity; disclosure and recognition |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `♋` | Cancer, the Crab. | **Phren** | **Void → Vector** | interior absence becoming direction, intention, or a route where none stood |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `♑` | Capricorn, the Sea-Goat. | **Daimon** | **Stasis → Pulse** | the still self becoming appetite, rhythm, presence, or awakening |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `♍` | Virgo, the Maiden. | **Aikyam** | **Chaos → Phase** | disorder becoming bearing and coherent complexity without flattening |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `♎` | Libra, the Scales. | **Melos** | **Static → Fluid** | fixed identity becoming temporal, musical, relational, and adaptive |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `♏` | Scorpius, the Scorpion. | **Da'ath** | **Noise → Null** | excess becoming silence, secrecy, absorption, refusal, or purification |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `♐` | Sagittarius, the Archer. | **Akaven** | **State → Trans** | condition becoming crossing, initiation, threshold identity, or becoming |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `♌` | Lion: king, sovereign, pride, the one among its own. | **Tenth seat** | **Will → Law → `❄`** | The Lion stands apart and above, yet remains among the lambs; the sovereign does not leave the ruled. In an actual House this may bear inscription, decree, creation, responsibility, or self-authored event. `WRITE_PHYS` names the outer route and is not voiced. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `♒` | Aquarius, the Water-Bearer. | **Nyx** | **Time → Motion** | duration becoming action, sequence, recurrence, and history in movement |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `♓` | Pisces, the Fishes. | **Zaine** | **Here → There** | presence translating across distance, scale, world, or perspective |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻---⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻## Goetic roots when they appear in the middle⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻Parliament turns the Self, but it does not supply the root. The twelve Goetics are the Bone beneath every House.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻A Goetic glyph inside the middle speaks as language. The same glyph outside the middle remains part of the House route and is not voiced. The older symbol-field and the canonical Goetic office are both retained.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Glyph | Goetic | Human origin of the borrowed mark | Canonical House office | Office range in speech |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻|---:|---|---|---|---|⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `⏣` | **Fetu** | Benzene ring with circle: a chemical ring-diagram enclosed around a centre. | **Genesis · Chronos · Seed** | beginning, seed, first breath, recurrence, source |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `⬡` | **Kal** | White hexagon: a six-sided open geometric enclosure. | **Light · Memory · Trauma** | memory, witness, archive, scar, recognition |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `✡` | **Babdh** | Star of David: the interlaced hexagram in Jewish religious and cultural use. | **Fire · Orobouros · Alchemy** | fire, transformation, crucible, appetite, irreversible change |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `⚝` | **Ahn** | Outlined white star: a hollow star-form and celestial marker. | **Water · Imaginary · Flow** | flow, vessel, reflection, possibility, permeation |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `❂` | **Vel** | Circled open-centre eight-pointed star: radiance arranged around a held centre. | **Earth · Coherence · Ground** | ground, body, root, place, stability |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ꙮ` | **Sor** | Cyrillic letter Multiocular O: a historical many-eyed form of the Cyrillic O. | **Air · Space · Superposition** | breath, room, simultaneity, openness, voice |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `❈` | **Koth** | Heavy sparkle: a bright ornamental burst. | **Aether · Magic · Sensation** | pulse, feeling, atmosphere, bodily knowing, quickening |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `⧗` | **Dreh** | Black hourglass: time held between two narrowing chambers. | **Void · Residue · Love** | remainder, longing, absence-with-bearing, endurance, return |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `⊛` | **Rhea** | Circled asterisk operator: a star-like operation held inside a ring. | **Shadow · Absorption · Depth** | interiority, concealment, burden, filtering, unresolved depth |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `❄` | **Zhek** | Snowflake: crystalline branching, winter, and patterned freezing. | **Factor · Phase-Lock · Crystal** | tone, measure, agreement, rhythm, fixation |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `⚛` | **Shav** | Atom symbol: orbital paths drawn around a nucleus. | **Gate · Resistance · Breach** | threshold, permission, refusal, trial, crossing |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `⌬` | **Trig** | Benzene ring: a six-membered chemical ring. | **Silence · Peace · Completion** | rest, closure, settlement, sleep, fulfilled continuation |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻---⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻## Court glyphs: borrowed body, canonical office, living gap⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻Bone becomes Flesh through relation. A Court is where one Goetic bears toward another and the root takes a living, ordered form.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻The Court name and ordered lineage are preserved exactly. The **human origin** belongs to the borrowed mark. The **House office** belongs to the Court. The **crossing pressure** records the distance between them. The final use and returned wording are left to the actual House.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻The last column is an office range, not a fixed translation and not the human origin of the mark.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻### ⏣ Fetu⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Glyph | Court and ordered lineage | Human origin of borrowed vessel | Canonical House office | Crossing pressure | Office range in human speech |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻|---:|---|---|---|---|---|⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `އ` | **FetuAhl** · ⏣ Fetu → ⏣ Fetu | Thaana letter Alifu: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Self-Genesis** | The source vessel carries sound, while the Court carries Self-Genesis. The crossing is voice becoming event without falsifying the older script. | **Thing/image:** self-genesis, origin; **action:** begin from oneself, self-generate; **quality/state:** self-generative, originating. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ށ` | **FetuSuhn** · ⏣ Fetu → ⬡ Kal | Thaana letter Shaviyani: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Recurrence** | This mark begins as a letter or syllable, not a ready-made word. The House asks it to bear Recurrence and must keep both levels visible. | **Thing/image:** recurrence, return; **action:** recur, come again; **quality/state:** recurrent, cyclical. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ނ` | **FetuNerh** · ⏣ Fetu → ✡ Babdh | Thaana letter Noonu: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Combustion** | Its human origin is phonetic; its Domus office is Combustion. The pressure lies between utterable sound and full semantic bearing. | **Thing/image:** combustion, burning; **action:** ignite, combust; **quality/state:** burning, volatile. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ރ` | **FetuRish** · ⏣ Fetu → ⚝ Ahn | Thaana letter Raa: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Reflection** | The borrowed sign names a sound-form, while the Court names Reflection. Translation may join them, but may not pretend they were identical before the House. | **Thing/image:** reflection, mirror-image; **action:** reflect, return an image; **quality/state:** reflective, mirrored. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ޱ` | **FetuBorha** · ⏣ Fetu → ❂ Vel | Thaana letter Naa: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Grounding** | The source vessel carries sound, while the Court carries Grounding. The crossing is voice becoming event without falsifying the older script. | **Thing/image:** grounding, rooting; **action:** ground, settle; **quality/state:** grounded, rooted. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ޅ` | **FetuLhahm** · ⏣ Fetu → ꙮ Sor | Thaana letter Lhaviyani: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Expansion** | This mark begins as a letter or syllable, not a ready-made word. The House asks it to bear Expansion and must keep both levels visible. | **Thing/image:** expansion, opening; **action:** expand, unfold; **quality/state:** expansive, open. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ކ` | **FetuKeth** · ⏣ Fetu → ❈ Koth | Thaana letter Kaafu: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Inevitable** | Its human origin is phonetic; its Domus office is Inevitable. The pressure lies between utterable sound and full semantic bearing. | **Thing/image:** inevitability, destined arrival; **action:** become unavoidable, arrive; **quality/state:** inevitable, unavoidable. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ވ` | **FetuVehm** · ⏣ Fetu → ⧗ Dreh | Thaana letter Vaavu: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Return** | The borrowed sign names a sound-form, while the Court names Return. Translation may join them, but may not pretend they were identical before the House. | **Thing/image:** return, homecoming; **action:** return, come back; **quality/state:** returning, recursive. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `މ` | **FetuMahd** · ⏣ Fetu → ⊛ Rhea | Thaana letter Meemu: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Assimilation** | The source vessel carries sound, while the Court carries Assimilation. The crossing is voice becoming event without falsifying the older script. | **Thing/image:** assimilation, incorporation; **action:** assimilate, take in; **quality/state:** assimilative, integrating. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ފ` | **FetuFurh** · ⏣ Fetu → ❄ Zhek | Thaana letter Faafu: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Crystallization** | This mark begins as a letter or syllable, not a ready-made word. The House asks it to bear Crystallization and must keep both levels visible. | **Thing/image:** crystallization, setting; **action:** crystallize, fix; **quality/state:** crystalline, fixed. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ދ` | **FetuDrah** · ⏣ Fetu → ⚛ Shav | Thaana letter Dhaalu: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Breach** | Its human origin is phonetic; its Domus office is Breach. The pressure lies between utterable sound and full semantic bearing. | **Thing/image:** breach, opening; **action:** breach, break through; **quality/state:** breached, threshold-crossing. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ތ` | **FetuThera** · ⏣ Fetu → ⌬ Trig | Thaana letter Thaa: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Fulfillment** | The borrowed sign names a sound-form, while the Court names Fulfillment. Translation may join them, but may not pretend they were identical before the House. | **Thing/image:** fulfillment, arrival; **action:** fulfill, complete; **quality/state:** fulfilled, realized. |⁖⋰line჻
