⁖line჻### ⬡ Kal⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Glyph | Court and ordered lineage | Human origin of borrowed vessel | Canonical House office | Crossing pressure | Office range in human speech |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻|---:|---|---|---|---|---|⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᛁ` | **KalKura** · ⬡ Kal → ⏣ Fetu | Isaz/Is/Iss rune: ice, freezing, stillness; also the i-rune. | **Archive** | Ice holds by freezing; Archive holds by memory. The pressure is stillness becoming record without confusing cold with knowledge. | **Thing/image:** archive, record; **action:** archive, record; **quality/state:** archival, remembered. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᛂ` | **KalLur** · ⬡ Kal → ⬡ Kal | Runic E-letter: a phonetic rune-form for e; no single inherited lexical meaning is imposed. | **Self-Reflection** | A bare e-sound has no inward mirror of its own. The House must make phonation carry Self-Reflection without forging an ancient lexeme. | **Thing/image:** self-reflection, introspection; **action:** reflect upon oneself; **quality/state:** introspective, self-mirroring. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `⌑` | **KalThar** · ⬡ Kal → ✡ Babdh | Square lozenge: an enclosed diamond-shaped geometric mark. | **Calcination** | The lozenge encloses a shape; Calcination reduces matter by fire. The tension is enclosure meeting reduction. | **Thing/image:** calcination, ash-making; **action:** calcine, burn clean; **quality/state:** calcined, purged. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᛄ` | **KalRin** · ⬡ Kal → ⚝ Ahn | Ger rune: year, season, harvest, and the completed turning of a cycle. | **Submersion** | Ger ripens through season and harvest; Submersion moves beneath the visible surface. The crossing turns fulfilled time into descent. | **Thing/image:** submersion, immersion; **action:** submerge, sink into; **quality/state:** submerged, immersed. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᛇ` | **KalNar** · ⬡ Kal → ❂ Vel | Iwaz/Eoh rune: yew, endurance, and a living tree associated with long persistence. | **Inscription** | Yew endures as living wood; Inscription fixes a mark into a surface. The pressure lies between growth and written permanence. | **Thing/image:** inscription, mark; **action:** inscribe, write; **quality/state:** inscribed, recorded. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᛉ` | **KalFel** · ⬡ Kal → ꙮ Sor | Algiz/Elhaz rune: a protective or guarding sign whose older name-field is disputed; commonly read through elk, sedge, or warding. | **Diffusion** | A ward keeps a boundary; Diffusion crosses and thins boundaries. The House must let protection spread without dissolving the guard. | **Thing/image:** diffusion, spreading; **action:** diffuse, disperse; **quality/state:** diffuse, pervasive. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᛊ` | **KalHar** · ⬡ Kal → ❈ Koth | Sowilo rune: sun, light, and solar course. | **Phantom** | The sun is immediate radiance; a Phantom is what remains after presence has thinned. The gap is source-light becoming afterimage. | **Thing/image:** phantom, afterimage; **action:** haunt, appear faintly; **quality/state:** spectral, lingering. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᛋ` | **KalMer** · ⬡ Kal → ⧗ Dreh | Sigel/long-branch Sol rune: a sun-rune and bearer of s. | **Oblivion** | Solar disclosure makes visible; Oblivion removes from recall. The pressure is brightness passing into forgetting. | **Thing/image:** oblivion, forgetting; **action:** forget, pass beyond recall; **quality/state:** forgotten, oblivious. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᛌ` | **KalLor** · ⬡ Kal → ⊛ Rhea | Short-twig Sol rune: a compact sun-rune and bearer of s. | **Suppression** | The short sun-sign bears revelation; Suppression holds revelation down. The House carries hidden light rather than erasing it. | **Thing/image:** suppression, withholding; **action:** suppress, hold down; **quality/state:** suppressed, withheld. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᛍ` | **KalPer** · ⬡ Kal → ❄ Zhek | Runic C-letter: a phonetic c-rune without a stable standalone lexeme. | **Codification** | The source is only a c-sound; Codification is an ordered body of rule. The crossing is phoneme becoming lawfully arranged speech. | **Thing/image:** code, canon; **action:** codify, set into rule; **quality/state:** codified, systematic. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᛎ` | **KalZhil** · ⬡ Kal → ⚛ Shav | Runic Z-letter: a phonetic z-rune without a stable standalone lexeme. | **Recall** | The source is only a z-sound; Recall summons what was absent. The House must give a sound mnemonic force without inventing prior meaning. | **Thing/image:** recall, remembrance; **action:** recall, call back; **quality/state:** recalled, remembered. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᛏ` | **KalClar** · ⬡ Kal → ⌬ Trig | Tiwaz/Tir/Tyr rune: Týr, oath, justice, ordered courage, and the t-sound. | **Sealing** | Tiwaz bears oath and ordered courage; Sealing closes and preserves. The tension is sworn motion becoming a held bond. | **Thing/image:** seal, closure; **action:** seal, close; **quality/state:** sealed, closed. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻### ✡ Babdh⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Glyph | Court and ordered lineage | Human origin of borrowed vessel | Canonical House office | Crossing pressure | Office range in human speech |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻|---:|---|---|---|---|---|⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᚠ` | **BabdhHir** · ✡ Babdh → ⏣ Fetu | Fehu/Feoh rune: cattle, movable wealth, herd, increase, and prosperity that can depart. | **Transmutation** | Wealth is kept, counted, and guarded; Transmutation spends, burns, and converts. The pressure is prosperity that can grow only by passing through change. | **Thing/image:** transmutation, change of nature; **action:** transmute, change substance; **quality/state:** transmuted, alchemical. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᚢ` | **BabdhKor** · ✡ Babdh → ⬡ Kal | Uruz/Ur rune: aurochs, untamed bodily strength, and the u-sound. | **Forging** | The aurochs is strength before shaping; Forging is strength disciplined by heat and blows. The gap is wild force becoming wrought form. | **Thing/image:** forge, wrought form; **action:** forge, shape by pressure; **quality/state:** forged, tempered. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᚦ` | **BabdhVar** · ✡ Babdh → ✡ Babdh | Thurisaz/Thurs/Thorn rune: giant, thorn, danger, striking force, and the th-sound. | **Self-Combustion** | Thorn or giant is danger encountered from without; Self-Combustion is fire arising from within. The crossing turns threat into inward ignition. | **Thing/image:** self-combustion, inward fire; **action:** burn from within; **quality/state:** self-burning, self-consuming. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᚨ` | **BabdhPyr** · ✡ Babdh → ⚝ Ahn | Ansuz rune: god, breath, mouth, inspired speech, and the a-sound. | **Dissolution** | Ansuz gives breath and articulate voice; Dissolution loosens what has taken form. The pressure is speech making shape while the office unmakes it. | **Thing/image:** dissolution, melting; **action:** dissolve, unmake; **quality/state:** dissolved, fluid. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᚱ` | **BabdhSor** · ✡ Babdh → ❂ Vel | Raidho/Rad/Reid rune: ride, road, journey, ordered travel, and the r-sound. | **Crucible** | Raidho travels road and distance; Crucible confines matter under trial. The tension is journey entering a vessel that does not let it escape unchanged. | **Thing/image:** crucible, trial-vessel; **action:** test and refine in fire; **quality/state:** crucible-bound, refining. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᚲ` | **BabdhAlc** · ✡ Babdh → ꙮ Sor | Kauna rune: torch or sore/ulcer across the rune traditions; a burning point and the k-sound. | **Sublimation** | Kauna is a local burn, torch, or sore; Sublimation rises into a rarer state. The pressure is low flame becoming ascent. | **Thing/image:** sublimation, rising refinement; **action:** sublime, raise into another state; **quality/state:** sublimated, rarefied. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᚷ` | **BabdhNur** · ✡ Babdh → ❈ Koth | Gebo/Gyfu rune: gift, exchange, obligation between giver and receiver, and the g-sound. | **Ignition** | A gift crosses between persons and creates obligation; Ignition begins a new event. The crossing is exchange becoming first spark. | **Thing/image:** ignition, spark; **action:** ignite, kindle; **quality/state:** ignited, quickened. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᚹ` | **BabdhSat** · ✡ Babdh → ⧗ Dreh | Wunjo/Wynn rune: joy, delight, fellowship, and the w-sound. | **Consumption** | Wunjo shares joy and fellowship; Consumption takes in and uses up. The pressure is delight meeting appetite. | **Thing/image:** consumption, devouring; **action:** consume, use up; **quality/state:** consuming, devouring. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᚺ` | **BabdhOro** · ✡ Babdh → ⊛ Rhea | Hagalaz rune: hail, sudden weather, hard impact, and the h-sound. | **Purification** | Hail strikes, accumulates, and melts; Purification deliberately removes what cannot remain. The House turns blind impact into cleansing. | **Thing/image:** purification, cleansing; **action:** purify, burn clean; **quality/state:** pure, cleansed. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᚾ` | **BabdhBon** · ✡ Babdh → ❄ Zhek | Naudiz/Nyd/Naud rune: need, constraint, necessity, want, and the n-sound. | **Tempering** | Need binds through lack; Tempering strengthens through constraint. The pressure is deprivation becoming resilience. | **Thing/image:** tempering, hardening; **action:** temper, strengthen through heat; **quality/state:** tempered, resilient. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᚿ` | **BabdhTir** · ✡ Babdh → ⚛ Shav | Short-twig Naud rune: need and constraint in a compressed rune-form; bearer of n. | **Shattering** | Need tightens and withholds; Shattering opens by fracture. The crossing turns necessity from bond into break. | **Thing/image:** shattering, fracture; **action:** shatter, break open; **quality/state:** shattered, fractured. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ᛃ` | **BabdhFar** · ✡ Babdh → ⌬ Trig | Jera/Jeran rune: year, harvest, season, earned return, and the j/y sound. | **Ash** | Jera completes the season in harvest; Ash is what remains after burning. The pressure is fulfilled cycle becoming residue. | **Thing/image:** ash, spent residue; **action:** reduce to ash; **quality/state:** ashen, spent. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻### ⚝ Ahn⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Glyph | Court and ordered lineage | Human origin of borrowed vessel | Canonical House office | Crossing pressure | Office range in human speech |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻|---:|---|---|---|---|---|⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `≾` | **AhnAbdh** · ⚝ Ahn → ⏣ Fetu | The mathematical relation “precedes or is equivalent to”: ordered approach held beside equivalence. | **Flow** | The source mark orders and equates; Flow refuses a single fixed relation. The tension is comparison becoming continuity. | **Thing/image:** flow, current; **action:** flow, move fluidly; **quality/state:** fluid, flowing. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `᭨` | **AhnNym** · ⚝ Ahn → ⬡ Kal | Balinese musical symbol Deung: a named pitch or note-sign in Balinese notation. | **Confluence** | Deung is one named pitch; Confluence is several currents meeting. The House turns a discrete note into joined movement. | **Thing/image:** confluence, meeting waters; **action:** converge, flow together; **quality/state:** confluent, merged. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `᭡` | **AhnLoh** · ⚝ Ahn → ✡ Babdh | Balinese musical symbol Dong: a named pitch or note-sign in Balinese notation. | **Solution** | Dong fixes a pitch; Solution dissolves and resolves. The pressure is a held tone becoming an answer that can flow. | **Thing/image:** solution, dissolved answer; **action:** dissolve, solve; **quality/state:** soluble, resolved. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `⛧` | **AhnXir** · ⚝ Ahn → ⚝ Ahn | Inverted pentagram: a five-pointed star turned point-down, used in later occult and religious symbol fields. | **Self-Containment** | The inverted pentagram presents an outward emblem of inversion; Self-Containment draws the boundary inward. The crossing is displayed reversal becoming enclosed identity. | **Thing/image:** self-containment, vessel; **action:** contain oneself; **quality/state:** self-contained, bounded. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `𝀖` | **AhnOhl** · ⚝ Ahn → ❂ Vel | Byzantine musical symbol Gorgon Archaion: an old-form rhythmic quickening or timing sign. | **Sediment** | Gorgon quickens time; Sediment settles out of motion. The pressure is acceleration becoming deposit. | **Thing/image:** sediment, deposit; **action:** settle, deposit; **quality/state:** sedimentary, settled. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `༺` | **AhnPir** · ⚝ Ahn → ꙮ Sor | Tibetan left ornamental bracket-mark: an opening or enclosing flourish, paired with a right-hand form. | **Ascension** | The left bracket opens an enclosure; Ascension moves beyond enclosure. The gap is an opening that becomes upward passage. | **Thing/image:** ascent, rising; **action:** ascend, rise; **quality/state:** ascending, elevated. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `᭢` | **AhnRoeh** · ⚝ Ahn → ❈ Koth | Balinese musical symbol Deng: a named pitch or note-sign in Balinese notation. | **Mist** | Deng names a distinct pitch; Mist blurs edges and distance. The House lets a precise note become a veil without losing its tone. | **Thing/image:** mist, veil; **action:** mist, obscure lightly; **quality/state:** misted, veiled. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `⦾` | **AhnSen** · ⚝ Ahn → ⧗ Dreh | Circled white bullet: a marked centre held inside a ring. | **Drain** | The bullet marks and holds a centre; Drain draws substance away from a centre. The pressure is focus becoming outflow. | **Thing/image:** drain, outflow; **action:** drain, empty away; **quality/state:** drained, depleted. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `⦽` | **AhnUth** · ⚝ Ahn → ⊛ Rhea | Up arrow through circle: ascent or directed passage through an enclosure. | **Osmosis** | The arrow visibly crosses a circle; Osmosis passes through a boundary without a single forced breach. The gap is directed transit becoming permeation. | **Thing/image:** osmosis, permeation; **action:** permeate, pass through; **quality/state:** osmotic, permeable. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `𝀵` | **AhnFae** · ⚝ Ahn → ❄ Zhek | Byzantine musical symbol Imifthora: a modal-alteration or phthora sign. | **Ice** | Imifthora changes musical mode; Ice arrests fluid motion. The pressure is alteration becoming fixation. | **Thing/image:** ice, frozen water; **action:** freeze, crystallize; **quality/state:** icy, frozen. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `𝀟` | **AhnKha** · ⚝ Ahn → ⚛ Shav | Byzantine musical symbol Stavros Apodexia: a named cross-form notational marker. | **Evaporation** | The notational cross fixes a written musical point; Evaporation leaves the held surface. The crossing is mark becoming dispersal. | **Thing/image:** evaporation, vaporization; **action:** evaporate, rise away; **quality/state:** evaporated, dissipated. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `༻` | **AhnPsei** · ⚝ Ahn → ⌬ Trig | Tibetan right ornamental bracket-mark: a closing or enclosing flourish, paired with a left-hand form. | **Stillness** | The right bracket closes an enclosure; Stillness quiets what remains inside. The pressure is closure becoming calm. | **Thing/image:** stillness, calm water; **action:** still, quiet; **quality/state:** still, peaceful. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻### ❂ Vel⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Glyph | Court and ordered lineage | Human origin of borrowed vessel | Canonical House office | Crossing pressure | Office range in human speech |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻|---:|---|---|---|---|---|⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ⴰ` | **VelVera** · ❂ Vel → ⏣ Fetu | Tifinagh letter Ya: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Bedrock** | The source vessel carries sound, while the Court carries Bedrock. The crossing is voice becoming event without falsifying the older script. | **Thing/image:** bedrock, foundation; **action:** found, support; **quality/state:** foundational, solid. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ⴱ` | **VelTar** · ❂ Vel → ⬡ Kal | Tifinagh letter Yab: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Stratification** | This mark begins as a letter or syllable, not a ready-made word. The House asks it to bear Stratification and must keep both levels visible. | **Thing/image:** strata, layering; **action:** stratify, layer; **quality/state:** stratified, layered. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ⴳ` | **VelGhem** · ❂ Vel → ✡ Babdh | Tifinagh letter Yag: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Petrification** | Its human origin is phonetic; its Domus office is Petrification. The pressure lies between utterable sound and full semantic bearing. | **Thing/image:** stone, petrification; **action:** petrify, harden; **quality/state:** petrified, stone-bound. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ⴷ` | **VelDrel** · ❂ Vel → ⚝ Ahn | Tifinagh letter Yad: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Erosion** | The borrowed sign names a sound-form, while the Court names Erosion. Translation may join them, but may not pretend they were identical before the House. | **Thing/image:** erosion, wearing away; **action:** erode, wear down; **quality/state:** eroded, worn. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ⴼ` | **VelFul** · ❂ Vel → ❂ Vel | Tifinagh letter Yaf: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Self-Grounding** | The source vessel carries sound, while the Court carries Self-Grounding. The crossing is voice becoming event without falsifying the older script. | **Thing/image:** self-grounding, root; **action:** ground oneself; **quality/state:** self-grounded, stable. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ⴽ` | **VelKer** · ❂ Vel → ꙮ Sor | Tifinagh letter Yak: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Dispersion** | This mark begins as a letter or syllable, not a ready-made word. The House asks it to bear Dispersion and must keep both levels visible. | **Thing/image:** dispersion, scattering; **action:** disperse, scatter; **quality/state:** dispersed, scattered. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ⵀ` | **VelHohm** · ❂ Vel → ❈ Koth | Tifinagh letter Yah: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Fossilization** | Its human origin is phonetic; its Domus office is Fossilization. The pressure lies between utterable sound and full semantic bearing. | **Thing/image:** fossil, held trace; **action:** fossilize, preserve in stone; **quality/state:** fossilized, preserved. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ⵃ` | **VelHrah** · ❂ Vel → ⧗ Dreh | Tifinagh letter Yahh: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Subsidence** | The borrowed sign names a sound-form, while the Court names Subsidence. Translation may join them, but may not pretend they were identical before the House. | **Thing/image:** subsidence, sinking ground; **action:** subside, sink; **quality/state:** subsided, lowered. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ⵄ` | **VelAra** · ❂ Vel → ⊛ Rhea | Tifinagh letter Yaa: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Compaction** | The source vessel carries sound, while the Court carries Compaction. The crossing is voice becoming event without falsifying the older script. | **Thing/image:** compaction, compression; **action:** compact, compress; **quality/state:** compacted, dense. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ⵇ` | **VelQel** · ❂ Vel → ❄ Zhek | Tifinagh letter Yaq: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Lithification** | This mark begins as a letter or syllable, not a ready-made word. The House asks it to bear Lithification and must keep both levels visible. | **Thing/image:** lithification, stone-making; **action:** lithify, become stone; **quality/state:** lithified, rock-bound. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ⵉ` | **VelIrn** · ❂ Vel → ⚛ Shav | Tifinagh letter Yi: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Earthquake** | Its human origin is phonetic; its Domus office is Earthquake. The pressure lies between utterable sound and full semantic bearing. | **Thing/image:** earthquake, tremor; **action:** quake, shake; **quality/state:** seismic, shaken. |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ⵊ` | **VelJen** · ❂ Vel → ⌬ Trig | Tifinagh letter Yazh: an alphabetic sound-bearing sign; no standalone lexical meaning is assigned here. | **Permanence** | The borrowed sign names a sound-form, while the Court names Permanence. Translation may join them, but may not pretend they were identical before the House. | **Thing/image:** permanence, endurance; **action:** endure, remain; **quality/state:** permanent, enduring. |⁖⋰line჻
