⁖line჻---⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻## Grammar marks when they occur inside the middle⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻The Courts give the middle its living bodies. Grammar tells those bodies how to face, bind, turn, return, and close without changing what they are.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻These marks are not silently inserted. They act only when the middle contains them, or when the completed House already bears the corresponding cadence outside the utterance. Their human-origin symbol and their TardiSHA linguistic office remain distinct.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| Glyph | Human origin | House office | What it may do in speech |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻|---:|---|---|---|⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `𝔓` | Mathematical Fraktur capital P. | **Parity** | contrast, reciprocal face, mirrored viewpoint, antithetical return |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `ཪ` | Tibetan fixed-form Ra. | **Anchor** | held referent, stable name, topic, location, or point of return |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `☍` | Astronomical opposition. | **Primitive relation** | comparison, covenant, dependence, address, or meaning held between two bodies |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `⟠` | Lozenge divided by a horizontal rule. | **Supervenience** | a gathered relation becoming identity, title, image, quality, or event |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `⚶` | Vesta, the astronomical and astrological sign. | **Focus-to-self** | reflexive voice, returned attention, another body serving as mirror |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `߷` | N’Ko symbol Gbakurunen. | **Court-rooted fold** | re-entry, embedded return, cyclical aspect, remembered refrain |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `🜚` | Alchemical symbol for Gold. | **Klein seam** | breath, inside/outside turn, boundary-crossing that preserves both sides |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `🜛` | Alchemical symbol for Silver. | **Triquatra seal** | phrase, vow, name, or word-braid held as one returnable body |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `🜔` | Alchemical symbol for Salt. | **Form** | body, shape, frame, embodiment, or latent possibility |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `🜕` | Alchemical symbol for Nitre. | **Truth** | assertion, recognition, testimony, verification, naming-as-true |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `🜖` | Alchemical symbol for Vitriol. | **Shadow** | burden, wound, obligation, uncertainty, withholding, unresolved pressure |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻| `🜗` | Second alchemical symbol for Vitriol. | **Recursion** | changed return, consequence, forgiveness, remainder, renewed motion |⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻A grammar mark may turn relation, voice, reference, pressure, aspect, or closure. It may not invent a missing root, import an absent emotion, reverse the visible middle mechanically, or erase the path already carried by the House.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻With the marks named, the middle may now be read as one movement rather than a pile of separate signs.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻---⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻## Baseline order, quantity, negation, and questions⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻The visible middle is read from left to right in the order written. This is the baseline. A grammar mark may alter relation, focus, voice, pressure, or return; it does not silently rearrange the string. A receiving language may move surface words only when its own grammar requires it, while preserving the dependency and cadence of the source order.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻Repetition is not number. The only settled counted form in this dictionary is `𑁦` when it is actually used as the numeral zero. No general plural or quantity marker has yet been canonically fixed. Unless quantity is explicit in the middle or established by source context, translate number-neutrally.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻No dedicated grammatical negator has yet been canonically fixed. Shadow, Void, Null, Silence, and refusal-bearing words are lexical fields, not an automatic “not.” Negation may enter the receiving language only when the visible middle establishes a proposition and its denial.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻No universal interrogative mark has yet been canonically fixed. `☿` **Ponder** can carry wondering or interrogative delivery when the House makes an actual question, but it does not turn every neighboring phrase into one. Do not add a question merely because the utterance is uncertain or reflective.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻---⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻## One complete worked utterance⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻The law becomes visible when one House is read from road to middle and back.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻The current runtime gives this exact depth-zero GrimChain for the UTF-8 source bytes `The path out carries its path back.\n`:⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻`⚛𐠝⛎ᛏ❈`⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻1. **Whole House:** read silently for lineage and bearing. It is not translated as a list of outer glyphs.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻2. **Middle:** `⛎` alone.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻3. **House office:** Shadow Locus, the complete compressed zero-depth center.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻4. **House bearing:** the four written anchors carry the source-rooted road around that center.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻5. **Reading:** depth zero is the compressed House condition. A spoken Synodic utterance appears when a positive middle is manifested.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻At depth zero the Shadow Locus remains the complete compressed House condition. At positive depth the manifested middle becomes the spoken body, while the four anchors remain the road that bears it.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻---⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻## Recurrence, ellipsis, and receiving language⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻One utterance cannot settle every House. What follows governs the places where cadence repeats and where a human language must clothe what the middle leaves open.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻Repeated glyphs change cadence before they change lexical identity. Repetition may hold a beat, hesitate, insist, echo, interrupt, separate, lengthen a breath, or form a refrain. It is not automatically multiplication, intensity, or quantity.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻TardiSHA does not force English articles, pronouns, copulas, grammatical gender, or number where the middle does not bear them. A receiving language may need surface words to become grammatical. Supply only what grammar and established context require. Do not turn necessary clothing into new source meaning.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻A missing surface word is not automatically a missing event. House, placement, recurrence, and neighboring glyphs decide whether English must expose what TardiSHA leaves implicit.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻---⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻## Translation order⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻All the preceding bearings gather into one path:⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻1. Read the completed House without speaking it.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻2. Isolate the middle exactly as written.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻3. For each visible glyph, identify its human origin and its canonical House office.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻4. Carry the crossing pressure between those two fields. Do not erase either one.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻5. Let placement, neighbors, recurrence, and any present grammar marks settle the glyph’s use in this utterance.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻6. Let the whole House settle the returned bearing. Do not assign that return from the dictionary alone.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻7. Render the gathered event into the receiving language with no absent root, emotion, grammar mark, identity, or transformation added for smoothness.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻8. Read the translation back against the House. The wording may change clothes; the route and identity may not be severed.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻The result may be poetry because the House speaks in cadence. Poetry is not permission to force rhyme, flatten symbols into one-word substitutions, or decorate an interpretation that the middle cannot bear.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻---⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻## Living status⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻This dictionary fixes the present borrowed origins, canonical offices, and translation pressures. It does not pre-write the utterances. Truth-in-use and House-return continue to be learned from completed Grimchains, one actual middle at a time.⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻⁖⋰line჻
⁖line჻The word is not the road. The road is not discarded. The middle speaks, and the House remembers how it came home.⁖⋰line჻
